## Context

Prove design sections 3–6 and 10 on small fixtures before mass migration; existing consumers must remain viable.

Design: `docs/jetp-backend-design.md`, revision 5. Plan: `docs/jetp-backend-implementation-plan.md`. Parent: 0760 (except the tracker itself, which belongs to 0725/#1333). Proposed work; no implementation authorized by filing.

## First test

Use equal raw IDs for a financial and implementation assertion, a late duplicate decision and a pending replacement. Typed joins must remain separate and an earlier cutoff must retain its earlier accepted state.

## Actions

Implement versioned validation/read interfaces, stable identity/relation/perimeter contracts, evidence tuples and bitemporal decision resolution. Include money-unit/precision and unsupported-closure fixtures. Add only the present study/frame/coverage contract fixtures needed to preserve research history; no empty future registries. Keep current CSV readers authoritative for unmigrated data.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Typed reference/cycle/cardinality validation rejects invalid fixtures
- [ ] Late acceptance, withdrawal and pending supersession preserve cutoff results
- [ ] Original values, whole-unit money and date roles survive round trips
- [ ] Compatibility reader supplies the existing MVP contract without unexplained output change

## Validation and recovery

Start implementation with the failing fixture. Run make check-fast and make lint; run the full make check for pipeline-surface diffs under AGENTS.md. Run the existing browser exercise for output/renderer changes. Cite exact fixture IDs and input/output commits in the PR. Preserve last accepted static output; candidate failure must not change canonical ownership or publish partial files. No deployment, estimator or PyPSA work is included in this ticket.

